From de54e74116e46352918a5edbe5b0823cedf188d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Triston Armstrong <tarmstrong95@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 21:46:34 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] drm: apple: apply VRR live in flush path instead of
 forced modeset

Forcing mode_changed when VRR_ENABLED toggles makes mutter's page-flip
atomic commit fail with EINVAL, so VRR could never actually be enabled
by userspace. Apply the adaptive-sync parameter live from the CRTC flush
path instead, which is safe for page-flip commits.

Also advertise vrr_capable from process_chunks/hotplug once modes are
parsed, so mutter exposes +vrr modes.

Includes temporary debug instrumentation (apple_ts_mode/ts_log based
present-flip and swap logging) for VRR investigation.
---
